<title>USA: TWA issued 3.8 mln shares in note exchange.</title>
<headline>TWA issued 3.8 mln shares in note exchange.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS, Mo. 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc said Thursday that, during July and August, it issued an aggregate of about 3.8 million shares of common stock in exchange for $40 million in notes.</p>
<p>The notes were part of its 12 percent senior secured reset notes due 1998 and were exchanged in privately negotiated transactions with two note holders, it added.</p>
<p>The company said, as a result of the exchanges, the aggregate outstanding principal amount of the 12 percent notes was cut to about $130 million from about $170 million.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
